In article <1993Aug20.180723.1@vxdesy.desy.de> pawlak@vxdesy.desy.de writes:
>This seems to be deliberate: the source in the appropriate place 
>contains a following comment:
>  /* No such thing as mindless players... */

No, what that comment means is that the code which deals with you eating the
brains of a mindless monster has no counterpart with a monster eating your
brains, so some of the code isn't parallep for those two cases.

The reason that the cause of death is 'unrecoverable' by life saving is that
it's not entirely clear how one should revive the player.  If you just bring
him back to life, his INT would still be less than 3 and he couldn't survive;
and amulets of lifesaving don't normally affect attributes.
